  "query_preview": "/Monday through Friday/...\nHigh pressure aloft will start to build over the area \nMonday/Monday night as an upper low exits the region across \nMontana into southern Canada. The higher pressure will bring \nwarmer air back into our CWA the rest of the week, with \ntemperatures approaching normal Wednesday and beyond. Drier air \nwill spread over the area Tuesday but moisture will be on the \nincrease again later in the week as the next upper low is \nforecast to move into postion near the Pacific Northwest coast \nwhile southwesterly flow aloft taps into moisture from the next \nwestward-moving hurricane in the Pacific subtropics. We \ntherefore have a 20 percent chance of showers and thunderstorms \nin the forecast as early as Wednesday afternoon near the Nevada \nborder, increasing to 20-40 percent across the forecast area \nThursday and Friday.",
